cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Dezh OS"
message: >-
  If you refer to Dezh in academic work, please cite it using this metadata.
  Dezh is a research prototype, not production software; the honest scope of
  every claim is recorded in docs/STATUS.md and the threat model.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Salimi
    given-names: Ali
    email: ali.salimi77@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/alisalimi77/Dezh"
url: "https://github.com/alisalimi77/Dezh"
abstract: >-
  Dezh is a bare-metal, intent-native and effect-accountable operating-system
  prototype written in Rust for RISC-V and x86_64. No program, app, service,
  package, driver or recovery path starts with ambient authority: every effect
  must be backed by an explicit capability, and the authority a task receives is
  the intersection of what it requested with the ceiling of the intent that
  authorized it. Every effect is recorded on an on-disk ledger with its actor,
  intent, derived capability and reversibility, and a whole agent mission can be
  rolled back - with the effects that genuinely cannot be undone refused by name
  rather than silently skipped.
keywords:
  - operating system
  - capability-based security
  - object capabilities
  - information flow control
  - effect accountability
  - reversibility
  - agent containment
  - microkernel
  - RISC-V
  - Rust
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.5-review"
date-released: "2026-08-18"
